WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:06.053
- Dear girl,

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:07.930
often times,

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:11.400
we women start to rise and
then certain people devise

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.560
a plan to disenfranchise.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.060
Whether it's our bodies or rights,

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:17.910
entice us with movements,

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.830
unite us through persecution,

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:22.140
make it seem like it's alright.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.490
Dear girl, open your eyes.

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:28.850
We have come so far, it's easy to resign.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:32.660
We've got equality, but public
policy shows the contrary.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:35.790
Honestly, no surprise since
we perpetuate rape culture,

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.331
separate locker room talk
in that one audio tape,

00:00:38.331 --> 00:00:39.260
that's great.

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:41.410
I get 78 cents to a man's dollar

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:43.710
while black and latino
women get even smaller.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.310
What should every girl know?

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:48.420
You are not some puppet in a puppet show.

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:51.880
Expose the double standards,
the hypocrisy, the hate.

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:53.750
It is never too late.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:56.880
This is the moment of
girls taking the reins.

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:59.450
It is time's up, it is me too,

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:02.050
it is everyone from me to you

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:05.400
who has spoken or stayed
silent, but strong.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:08.500
It is Emma Gonzales and Lena Waithe

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:10.860
from dodging bullets and dodging hate.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:14.240
Christine Blasey Ford and
every survivor that speaks

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:16.080
only to be met with intimidation,

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.630
investigation, and disbelief.

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:23.550
Dear girl, you will be believed.

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:26.940
If not by Senate floors and investigators,

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:28.390
we will hear you.

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:30.530
Dear girl, we will see you.

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:33.180
Dear girl, we will stand by you.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:38.750
For the survivor 3,000 miles
away or the one next door,

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:40.610
you are heard.

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:42.380
Justice will not always prevail,

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:45.370
but we will continue to
fight tooth and nail.

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:46.600
You are heard.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:49.830
So that our sisters and
daughters will never be asked,

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:51.300
rather, harassed

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:54.790
whether they wanted it,
regretted it, or just forgot.

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:58.930
Believe me, no one forgot.

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:04.740
Dear everyone, this moment is a movement.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:09.290
For every girl to reclaim
her place, win every race.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.450
For everyone out there, listen in.

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:13.730
The system is in demolition.

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:15.590
Gran ahold of your voice,

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:17.760
it is time to make a choice

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:22.190
to believe survivors,
to pay us all the same,

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:26.440
to give women of color equal
access and opportunity,

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:30.490
to protect the safety of
trans girls every day.

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:34.900
Make the choice to change the climate.

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:38.060
Make the choice to not stay silent.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:40.880
This is not just the day of the girl,

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:45.180
this is the future of girls.

00:02:46.609 --> 00:02:49.192
(somber music)

